# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Config de agente: local del operador, nunca del producto.
# .claude/ (reglas del proyecto, CLAUDE.md, hooks, settings.json) y su
# proyección .codex/ son la configuración con la que cada dev corre sus
# agentes: cambia por máquina, por arnés y por preferencia, y no describe el
# runtime que se publica. Se queda afuera de la historia de git.
# Los hooks propios SÍ viajan, por el patrón del ADR-0043: el artefacto
# revisable es scripts/agent-hook-block-destructive-bash.sh más el instalador
# scripts/install-hooks.sh, que lo symlinkea en .claude/hooks/ y .codex/hooks/.
# Por eso .codex/ sigue ignorado aunque hoy no exista en el checkout: el
# instalador lo vuelve a crear en cada clon.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.codex/

# ── Go (producto) ──
# Binarios compilados y artefactos de build.
/aisotropyd
# Dev-tool binaries dropped by `go build ./cmd/X` without -o (run these via `go run`).
/bitrate-harness
/skill-import
/embed-bench
/bin/
*.exe
*.out
*.test
# Compiled example bots: each example is its own module, so `go build ./...`
# (or `go build .`) drops a binary named after the directory next to its go.mod.
# Those are build artifacts — never commit them. When you add an example, add a
# line here for its binary (one per module; gitignore can't match "extensionless
# file named after its dir" generically).
/examples/weatherbot/weatherbot
/examples/helpdesk/helpdesk
# Stray dev-console binary (go build ./cmd/x → ./x).
/x
# Cobertura
*.cover
coverage.out

# ── Entorno / secretos ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Runtime config FILE (aisotropy/runtimeconfig.go, ADR-0040) — an operator's local,
# environment-specific copy, never a repo artifact. This is the SECOND barrier, not
# the defense: `git add -f` walks straight past .gitignore, so per ADR-0072 the
# loader itself REFUSES to read any secret-bearing key from these files.
# The committed reference `aisotropy.runtime.example.yaml` is deliberately kept
# (negated below) — it carries no secret keys, guarded by
# TestExampleRuntimeConfig_IsRealAndInert.
aisotropy.runtime*.yaml
aisotropy.runtime*.yml
aisotropy.runtime*.toml
!aisotropy.runtime.example.yaml

# ── SO / editor ──
.DS_Store

# Raw brainstorm transcripts (source material, kept local, not published)
raw-notes/

# Third-party source cloned locally for study (not published)
external/

# stray benchmark binary if built without -o (use `go run ./bench/token-economy`)
/token-economy

# Rust build artifacts (sleep-cycle worker, ADR-0005)
/crates/**/target/
crates/*/target/
/examples/task-agent/task-agent
/examples/task-fanout/task-fanout
/examples/memory-sessions/memory-sessions
/examples/multi-tenant/multi-tenant
/examples/auth-scopes/auth-scopes
/examples/knowledge-rag/knowledge-rag
/examples/serve-http/serve-http
/examples/guardrail-policy/guardrail-policy
/examples/domain-assistant/domain-assistant

examples/graphbot/graphbot

# stray build artifacts (binaries built from cmd/* and bench/* into repo root)
/aisotropy-backup
/audit-verify
/load
/rag-quality
/wasm-vs-docker
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Arena runtime state (never commit) ──
arenas/live/*/.aisotropy-data
arenas/live/*/.aisotropy-data.arena-run-marker
arenas/live/*/.data

# Python bytecode (examples/ PoCs)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Compiled footprint/bench binaries. Go bakes ABSOLUTE build paths into the
# binary, so committing one publishes the builder's home directory and real name
# to anyone who runs `strings` on it — and a binary in git history cannot be
# removed without rewriting every commit after it. This repo already carries one
# such blob in history (arenas/adk-go/parity, 21.5 MB, found by the
# pre-publication audit); arenas/.gitignore was added reactively for that case.
# These patterns close the remaining class BEFORE a `git add -A` makes it
# permanent.
bench/footprint/*/adk-go-footprint
bench/footprint/*/*-footprint

# Runner artifacts and local working notes — regenerated or machine-local, and
# the same "untracked but not ignored" trap as the compiled binaries above: a
# single `git add -A` before publication would commit them permanently.
# The durable record stream: the ONLY source from which a board can be
# re-rendered, drift-checked or re-analysed at cell level. Gitignored because it
# is large and regenerated per run — but that also means git cannot recover it,
# and the runner APPENDS to it on every invocation, so a small debugging run
# mixes into a finished board. An Agnes board's 780 records were destroyed this
# way on 2026-07-28 (a failed `head -n -2` whose redirect emptied the file).
# scripts/arena-post-board.sh now archives it read-only as its FIRST action —
# archive the artefact before anything is allowed to touch it.
arenas/live/RESULTS.records.jsonl
# Read-only per-board archives written by arena-post-board.sh. Kept out of git
# for size; they are the local safety net, not the published evidence (RESULTS.md
# is, and it IS committed).
arenas/live/.records-archive/
CACHE.md

# Lista local de términos privados para scripts/pre-publication-sweep.sh (nunca se versiona)
.private-sweep-names
